IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art03-commencement`
IMPORT `je21-seat-1-making-and-commencement`
IMPORT `je21-seat-2-powers-and-effects`

-- je21-tests-independent-1: an independent test author's reading of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021), asserted against the exported questions of the row. Part 1 of 2: the Law itself (Article 26 and the endnotes) and Articles 1 to 8.
-- The first version of this file was one module of 887 lines (je21-tests-independent.l4); it was split by Article into two, and no assertion was lost: this part has 152 assertions and the other has 183, 335 in all.
-- Status: ASSUMED, NOT RULED. These are one reader's answers, decided from the text of the Law alone before any file of the encoding was opened; the owner of the Law has ruled on none of them.
-- Only the mapping of each decided answer onto an exported question (its inputs, and whether FALSE or a refusal is the answer) was made after the seat modules were read, and by the rule below, fixed before the run.
-- Where the text allows two readings and the author could not decide, the assertion is in the last section, carries "UNSURE" in its comment, and asserts the reading the author would take; a failure there is a triage item, not a verdict.
-- A failing assertion is a finding. After the first run of the whole file (335 assertions: 323 satisfied, 9 failed, 3 refused as a warning) each was triaged; the table is in NOTES.md section 10.3.
-- No expected value was edited to fit what the code answered. Four BECAUSE texts were corrected (the author's error, below), one assertion was moved to a registered alternative reading, and the rest were settled by changes to the encoding.
--
-- Citations in the comments are bare locators, "(src:N)", lines of the current text of the Law; none is a quotation, so none is a quote line.
-- Bracketed ids such as [C-01] are the author's scenario ids.
--
-- How a refusal is asserted. "#ASSERT REFUSED expr BECAUSE msg" needs msg to equal the refusal text exactly.
-- Where the refusal comes from the REFUSE written in the exported question itself, the BECAUSE text is that REFUSE copied verbatim.
-- Where the refusal can come from a rule module (not read by the author before this file was written), the assertion has no BECAUSE.
-- Author's error, corrected after the first run: four assertions on Article 9(2), 9(3) and 9(4) for legislation made on or before 28 Mar 2003 carried the BECAUSE of the exported question,
-- but the refusal that answers is raised by the rule module with a different text; each now carries the text actually raised, with a comment above it.
-- They refused, as decided; they had failed only on the message.
--
-- The author's rule for FALSE against REFUSE (fixed before the run):
--   FALSE when the Law states a limit in terms ("only if", "other than", "no later than", "limited to") or the question is whether an Article applies to something outside its stated scope;
--   a refusal when the question is whether something MAY be done, the Article gives permission only on conditions that are not met, and the Law says nothing else.
--
-- Decided but with no exported question to assert against (a coverage observation, not a finding):
--   Article 2(5), 11(5), 15(10), 17(6) and 23 (the States' powers to amend by Regulations); Articles 19 to 21 (the Office and delegation);
--   Article 15(2) and (3) (who sits on the Board, how it works); the Article 1 definition of "publish" (a paywalled site is not publication);
--   the wording of Article 2(1)(b) in each text (no exported question returns it); Article 15(9) with no last permitted day given (the input is required);
--   Article 11(1) with an instrument never laid; Article 3(1) for a silent provision of legislation made before 28 September 2021;
--   Article 3(2) with a stated time of day (the exports take no stated time); Article 12(3) with no stated consolidation date.

§ `Helpers`

-- Is the answer the value that says the Law was not in force on the day asked?
GIVEN a IS AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind: a yes-or-no answer is the not-in-force value` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN LEFT x THEN TRUE
    WHEN RIGHT y THEN FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind: a day answer is the not-in-force value` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN LEFT x THEN TRUE
    WHEN RIGHT y THEN FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN EITHER `Before the Law was in force` (MAYBE DATE)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind: a made-on answer is the not-in-force value` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN LEFT x THEN TRUE
    WHEN RIGHT y THEN FALSE

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Time of day`
`ind: the time` h m MEANS `Time of day` WITH `hour of the day` IS h, `minute of the hour` IS m

-- The seven facts of Article 1, in the order of the DECLARE:
-- a: Regulations, an Order or another instrument having legislative effect; b: made in Jersey; c: what it is made under; d: adopted by the States; e: relies on other legislation for its making; f: a provision of a UK Act or subordinate legislation made under one; g: registered in the Royal Court.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `What an instrument is made under`, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an instrument`
`ind: an instrument with` a b c d e f g MEANS
    `Facts about an instrument` WITH
        `it is Regulations, an Order or another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` IS a
        `it was made in Jersey` IS b
        `it is made under` IS c
        `it was adopted by the States` IS d
        `it relies on other legislation to empower its making` IS e
        `it is a provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act` IS f
        `it has been registered in the Royal Court` IS g

-- The steps toward making a Law: adopted on, sanctioned on, registered on, taxation draft declared under Article 12(1) of the 2019 Law.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE, b IS A MAYBE DATE, c IS A MAYBE DATE, d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Steps toward making a Law`
`ind: law steps` a b c d MEANS
    `Steps toward making a Law` WITH
        `it was adopted by the States Assembly on` IS a
        `it was sanctioned by Order in Council on` IS b
        `it was registered in the Royal Court on` IS c
        `it is a taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Article 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019` IS d

-- The steps toward making subordinate legislation: form, proposition adopted on, signed on, signed by the person responsible, made by a body, signed by a person acting in accordance with the body's procedure.
GIVEN f IS A `Form of legislation`, a IS A MAYBE DATE, s IS A MAYBE DATE, r IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Steps toward making subordinate legislation`
`ind: subordinate steps` f a s r b p MEANS
    `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` WITH
        `its form` IS f
        `the proposition containing it was adopted by the States Assembly on` IS a
        `it was signed on` IS s
        `it was signed by the person responsible for making it` IS r
        `it was made by a body` IS b
        `it was signed by a person acting in accordance with the procedural requirements of the body` IS p


§ `Fixtures`

`ind: the Law, adopted by the States, relying on nothing` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` FALSE TRUE `neither of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`ind: Regulations adopted by the States under a Law` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` TRUE TRUE `Jersey legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`ind: an Order signed by a Minister under a Law` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` TRUE TRUE `Jersey legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`ind: an instrument made in Jersey under a registered UK Order in Council` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` TRUE TRUE `UK extended legislation or an Order in Council registered in the Royal Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`ind: an instrument made outside Jersey under an unregistered UK Act` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` TRUE FALSE `neither of these` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`ind: a provision of a UK Act registered in the Royal Court` MEANS `ind: an instrument with` FALSE FALSE `neither of these` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

`ind: law steps, all three done` MEANS `ind: law steps` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2022 4 5)) (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12)) FALSE
`ind: law steps, adopted and sanctioned only` MEANS `ind: law steps` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2022 4 5)) NOTHING FALSE
`ind: law steps, sanctioned and registered only` MEANS `ind: law steps` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 4 5)) (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12)) FALSE
`ind: law steps, none done` MEANS `ind: law steps` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
`ind: law steps, all three done on one day` MEANS `ind: law steps` (JUST (YMD 2022 6 7)) (JUST (YMD 2022 6 7)) (JUST (YMD 2022 6 7)) FALSE
`ind: law steps, taxation draft declared, nothing else done` MEANS `ind: law steps` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE
`ind: law steps, taxation draft not declared, nothing else done` MEANS `ind: law steps` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
`ind: law steps, taxation draft declared, then sanctioned and registered` MEANS `ind: law steps` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 4 5)) (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12)) TRUE

§ `The Law itself: Article 26 and the endnotes`

-- Art 26 (src:223) with the endnote's commencement day (src:260-261) [T-01]: not in force on 27 Sep 2021.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 26 and the endnote (src:223, 260-261) [T-02]: in force on 28 Sep 2021, day level.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 28) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 26 [T-03]: in force on 29 Sep 2021.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 29) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 26 [T-04]: in force on 10 Jan 2024.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 10) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 26 [T-05]: in force on 11 Jan 2024.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 11) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 26 [T-09]: long before the Law, not in force.
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Vintages: the text of 28 Sep 2021 to 10 Jan 2024 (src:l_8_2021_20240110) and of 11 Jan 2024 on (src:268-270) [T-09]: nothing governs 27 Sep 2021.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS `the Law was not in force`
-- Vintages [T-02]: 28 Sep 2021 is the first day of the earlier text.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 28) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
-- Vintages [T-08]: 10 Jan 2024 is the last day of the earlier text.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 10) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
-- Vintages [T-05]: 11 Jan 2024 is the first day of the later text.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 11) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
-- Vintages [T-07]: a later day still has the later text.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2030 12 31) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
-- Vintages [T-06]: a day in the middle of the earlier text.
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2022 3 15) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`

§ `Article 1: what an instrument is`

-- Art 1 "Law" (src:15) [A-01]: adopted by the States, relies on no other legislation: a Law.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a Law?` `ind: the Law, adopted by the States, relying on nothing` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11) [A-08]: a Law is Jersey legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `ind: the Law, adopted by the States, relying on nothing` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12-14) [A-08]: a Law is not subordinate legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `ind: the Law, adopted by the States, relying on nothing` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Law" (src:15) [A-02]: Regulations adopted by the States under a Law rely on other legislation: not a Law.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a Law?` `ind: Regulations adopted by the States under a Law` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12-13) [A-02]: Regulations made in Jersey under Jersey legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `ind: Regulations adopted by the States under a Law` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11) [A-02]: subordinate legislation is Jersey legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `ind: Regulations adopted by the States under a Law` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12-13) [A-03]: an Order signed by a Minister under a Law.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `ind: an Order signed by a Minister under a Law` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Law" (src:15) [A-03]: an Order is not a Law.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a Law?` `ind: an Order signed by a Minister under a Law` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (b) (src:14) [A-04, A-05]: made in Jersey under a registered Order in Council or UK extended legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `ind: an instrument made in Jersey under a registered UK Order in Council` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "UK extended legislation" (src:28) [A-04]: an instrument made in Jersey is not itself a provision of a UK Act.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `ind: an instrument made in Jersey under a registered UK Order in Council` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12) [A-06]: made outside Jersey under an unregistered UK Act.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `ind: an instrument made outside Jersey under an unregistered UK Act` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11) [A-06]: not Jersey legislation either.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `ind: an instrument made outside Jersey under an unregistered UK Act` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "UK extended legislation" (src:28) [A-06]: not registered in the Royal Court, so not UK extended legislation.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `ind: an instrument made outside Jersey under an unregistered UK Act` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "UK extended legislation" (src:28) [A-07]: a UK Act provision registered in the Royal Court.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `ind: a provision of a UK Act registered in the Royal Court` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11, 16) [A-07]: "legislation" includes it, "Jersey legislation" does not.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `ind: a provision of a UK Act registered in the Royal Court` EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 1 "Law" (src:15) [A-07]: not a Law.
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a Law?` `ind: a provision of a UK Act registered in the Royal Court` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Article 2: how Jersey legislation is made`

-- Art 2(1), 2(4) (src:32-35, 42) [B-01]: all three steps done, asked on a day in 2022.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, all three done` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(4) (src:42) [B-01]: a Law is made on the day it was registered.
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, all three done` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12))
-- Art 2(1) (src:32-35) [B-02]: adopted and sanctioned but not registered: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(1), 2(4) [B-02]: not made, so no day it was made.
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT NOTHING
-- Art 2(1) (src:32-35) [B-03]: sanctioned and registered but not adopted: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, sanctioned and registered only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(1) [B-05]: no step done: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, none done` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(1), 2(4) [B-06]: all three on one day, made that day.
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 7) `ind: law steps, all three done on one day` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 6 7))
-- Art 2(2) (src:36) [B-07]: a taxation draft declared by Act of the States to have effect under Art 12(1) of the Public Finances (Jersey) Law 2019 is treated as made, with no sanction or registration.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, taxation draft declared, nothing else done` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(2) [B-09]: a taxation draft not so declared, nothing else done: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, taxation draft not declared, nothing else done` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(2), 2(1) [B-10]: declared, then sanctioned and registered: made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, taxation draft declared, then sanctioned and registered` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(2), 2(4) (src:36, 42) [B-11, U-11]: the day a taxation draft is treated as made is not stated; with no registration the day cannot be given.
#ASSERT REFUSED `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `ind: law steps, taxation draft declared, nothing else done`
-- Art 26 and the endnotes [T-01]: asked on 27 Sep 2021, the answer is the value that says the Law was not in force.
#ASSERT `ind: a yes-or-no answer is the not-in-force value` (`Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2021 9 27) `ind: law steps, all three done`) EQUALS TRUE
-- Vintages [T-04, T-05, T-10]: the same Law, asked on the last day of the earlier text.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2024 1 10) `ind: law steps, all three done` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Vintages [T-05, T-10]: the same Law, asked on the first day of the later text, same answer (the change in 2(1)(b) is editorial).
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2024 1 11) `ind: law steps, all three done` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Vintages [T-04, T-10]: the same incomplete Law, asked on the last day of the earlier text.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2024 1 10) `ind: law steps, adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Vintages [T-05, T-10]: the same incomplete Law, asked on the first day of the later text.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2024 1 11) `ind: law steps, adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(4) with the vintages [T-05]: the day made is the same under both texts.
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2024 1 11) `ind: law steps, all three done` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12))
-- Art 2(3)(a), 2(4) (src:38, 42) [B-12, B-14]: Regulations, proposition adopted 5 Jul 2022, never signed (signing is not a step for Regulations): made.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 8 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `Regulations` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 5)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(4) [B-12]: made on the day the proposition was adopted.
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 8 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `Regulations` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 5)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 7 5))
-- Art 2(3)(a) [B-13]: Regulations whose proposition has not been adopted: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 8 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `Regulations` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(3)(a) (src:38) [B-15]: Triennial Regulations adopted.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 8 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `Triennial Regulations` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 5)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(3)(a) (src:38) [B-16]: an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation, proposition adopted.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 8 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 5)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(3)(b)(i), 2(4) (src:39-40, 42) [B-17]: an Order signed by the person responsible on 9 Aug 2022.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Order` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(4) [B-17, B-22]: made on the day it was signed.
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Order` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9))
-- Art 2(3)(b) [B-18]: an Order not signed: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Order` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(3)(b)(i) [B-19]: an Order signed, but not by the person responsible and not by a body: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Order` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 2(3)(b)(ii) (src:41) [B-20]: an instrument of a body, signed by a person acting in accordance with its procedure.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Art 2(3)(b)(ii) [B-21]: signed by a person who did not act in accordance with the body's procedure: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 9 1) (`ind: subordinate steps` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- Art 26 [T-01]: asked on 27 Sep 2021 about subordinate legislation, the not-in-force value.
#ASSERT `ind: a yes-or-no answer is the not-in-force value` (`Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2021 9 27) (`ind: subordinate steps` `an Order` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 8 9)) TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE

§ `Article 3: when Jersey legislation comes into force`

-- Art 3(1)(b) (src:47) [C-01]: silent, other legislation, made 10 Jun 2022: in force from 11 Jun 2022.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 6 11)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-06]: made 31 Dec 2022, in force 1 Jan 2023.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 12 31) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2023 1 1)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-07]: made 28 Feb 2024 (leap year), in force 29 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2024 2 29)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-08]: made 28 Feb 2023, in force 1 Mar 2023.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2023 2 28) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2023 3 1)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-09]: made 29 Feb 2024, in force 1 Mar 2024.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2024 3 1)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-40]: made on the registration day 12 Apr 2022, in force 13 Apr 2022.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 4 12) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 4 13)
-- Art 3(1)(a) (src:46) [C-10]: legislation having effect only to commence other legislation, silent: in force when made, the same day.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 6 10)
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-14]: an Act of the States referred to in Art 2(2), silent: in force when made, the same day.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` (YMD 2022 6 10) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 6 10)
-- Art 3(1)(b), Art 26 [C-01]: asked as at 27 Sep 2021 the answer is the not-in-force value.
#ASSERT `ind: a day answer is the not-in-force value` (`On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2021 9 27)) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(1)(b) (src:47) [C-02]: silent, made 10 Jun 2022: not in force on 9 Jun 2022, any time of day.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 9) (`ind: the time` 12 0) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-03]: not in force on the day it was made, any time of day.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 23 59) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-05, U-06]: on the day after it was made, the Law says no instant, so a time of day is refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 11) (`ind: the time` 12 0)
-- Art 3(1)(b) [C-04]: in force at any time two days after it was made.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 12) (`ind: the time` 0 0) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(1)(a) (src:46) [C-11]: only-commencing legislation made 10 Jun 2022: not in force the day before.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 9) (`ind: the time` 23 59) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-12]: in force on the day after it was made.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 11) (`ind: the time` 0 0) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-13, U-08]: made on 10 Jun 2022 at a time not known: whether it is in force at midday on 10 Jun cannot be said.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) NOTHING (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 12 0)
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-10]: made at 14:30 on 10 Jun 2022; "when it is made" is 14:30, so not in force at 14:29.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) (JUST (`ind: the time` 14 30)) (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 14 29) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-10]: in force at 14:30 when made at 14:30.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) (JUST (`ind: the time` 14 30)) (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 14 30) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-10]: in force at 18:00 on the day made at 14:30.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 6 10) (JUST (`ind: the time` 14 30)) (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 18 0) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(1)(a) [C-14]: an Act referred to in 2(2), made at 14:30: not in force at 14:29.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` (YMD 2022 6 10) (JUST (`ind: the time` 14 30)) (YMD 2022 6 10) (`ind: the time` 14 29) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(6) (src:54) [C-34]: legislation that commenced on 27 Sep 2021 is not governed by Article 3.
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 27)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(6) [C-34]: or long before.
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2001 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(6) [C-35]: legislation that commenced on 29 Sep 2021 is governed by Article 3.
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 29)) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(6) [C-36]: legislation that has not yet commenced is governed by Article 3.
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(6) [C-35]: legislation commenced in 2024.
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2024 3 1)) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(3) (src:49) [C-22]: Regulations, no provision to the contrary: may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister.
#ASSERT `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(3) [C-23]: provision to the contrary: the Law does not say what follows.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 3(3) lets Regulations provide this unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say whether any other instrument can, or what follows where provision is made to the contrary"
-- Art 3(3) [C-24]: not Regulations: Article 3(3) gives nothing, and the Law says nothing else.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(3) lets Regulations provide this unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say whether any other instrument can, or what follows where provision is made to the contrary"
-- Art 3(4) (src:50) [C-25, C-26]: a Law or Regulations made under a Law, commencable by Act or Order on a specified day: different days, times or events for different provisions.
#ASSERT `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 3(4) [C-27, C-28]: a power to commence by some other instrument: the Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether any other power can name different days, times or events"
-- Art 3(4) [C-27]: not a Law or Regulations made under a Law: the Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether any other power can name different days, times or events"
-- Art 3(5)(a) (src:52) [C-30]: amending an uncommenced provision does not commence it.
#ASSERT `Does an amendment of uncommenced legislation commence it?` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 3(5)(b) (src:53) [C-31]: the amendment commences when the provision amended commences (1 Jul 2022).
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 1)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 7 1)
-- Art 3(5)(b) [C-32]: provision made otherwise: the day that provision gives.
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` (JUST (YMD 2022 7 1)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2022 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 9 1)
-- Art 3(5)(b) [C-31]: the provision amended has not commenced and nothing else gives a day: no day.
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 4: exercising a power before the legislation is in force`

-- Art 4(1)(a) (src:56-57) [D-04]: a power to make subordinate legislation, given by Jersey legislation, is covered.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1)(b) (src:58) [D-04]: a power to establish an entity.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to establish an entity` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1)(c) (src:59) [D-04]: a power to make an appointment.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to make an appointment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1)(d) (src:60) [D-04]: a power to give a notice or document.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to give a notice or document` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1)(e) (src:61) [D-04]: a power to prescribe a form.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to prescribe a form` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1)(f) (src:62) [D-04]: a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(1) (src:56) [D-05]: a power given by a UK Act is outside "any Jersey legislation": Article 4 does not cover it (a scope clause, rule FALSE).
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 4(1) (src:56-62) [D-04]: a power that is none of (a) to (f): not covered.
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 4(2) (src:63) [D-01]: legislation made but not in force, no provision to the contrary: the power may be exercised.
#ASSERT `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(2) [D-04]: the same for a power to establish an entity.
#ASSERT `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to establish an entity` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(2) [D-02]: the legislation has not been made: Article 4(2) gives no power; the Law says nothing else.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 4(2) [D-03]: provision to the contrary: Article 4(2) gives nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 4(2) [D-05]: a power given by something other than Jersey legislation: the Law says nothing about exercising it early.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 4(3) (src:64) [D-06]: coming into force on 30 Jun 2022, the day before the enabling provision (1 Jul 2022): barred.
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 6 30) (YMD 2022 7 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Art 4(3) [D-07]: coming into force on the same day as the enabling provision: not before it, so not barred.
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 7 1) (YMD 2022 7 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(3) [D-08]: the day after.
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 7 2) (YMD 2022 7 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 4(3) [D-06]: months before.
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2022 7 1) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Article 5: what a repeal or expiry leaves alone`

-- Art 5(2)(a) (src:68) [E-03]: validity of things done under the repealed legislation, Jersey legislation repealing Jersey legislation, no contrary provision.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2)(b) (src:69) [E-01, E-02]: accrued rights and liabilities.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2)(c) (src:70) [E-01]: amendments of other legislation made by the repealed legislation.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2)(d) (src:71) [E-01]: the previous operation of the repealed legislation.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `the previous operation of the repealed legislation, or anything done or permitted under it` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2)(e) (src:72) [E-05]: an investigation, proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to a right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability under it` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2)(f) (src:73) [E-04]: a penalty for an offence committed before the repeal.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(2) (src:67) [E-06]: provision to the contrary: Article 5(2) gives nothing; the Law says nothing else.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
-- Art 5(1) (src:66) [E-07]: what was repealed is not Jersey legislation (UK extended legislation): Article 5 does not apply.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
-- Art 5(1) (src:66) [V-14]: the repealing instrument is not Jersey legislation: Article 5 does not apply.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
-- Art 5(3) (src:74) [E-04, E-05]: a penalty or proceeding mentioned in paragraph (2) may go ahead as if not repealed.
#ASSERT `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(1) [E-07]: what was repealed is not Jersey legislation: the Law says nothing about proceedings either.
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(3) lets a proceeding about, or a penalty for, something mentioned in paragraph (2) go ahead as if the legislation had not been repealed when Article 5 applies, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- Art 5(4)(a) (src:76) [E-08]: the repeal of Law B, which had repealed Law A, does not revive A.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `legislation that was repealed` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(4)(b) (src:77) [E-09]: nor a rule of law that had been abolished.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `a rule of law that had been abolished` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(4)(c) (src:78) [E-10]: nor any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 5(4) (src:75) [E-11]: provision to the contrary: the Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `legislation that was repealed` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 5(4) stops a repeal reviving these things when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

§ `Article 6: repeal and re-enactment`

-- Art 6 (src:81) [F-01]: Jersey legislation repeals Jersey legislation and re-enacts a provision; the reference in other Jersey legislation; no contrary provision.
#ASSERT `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 6 [F-02]: the provision was repealed and not re-enacted: Article 6 says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
-- Art 6 [F-03]: provision to the contrary.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
-- Art 6 [F-04]: the reference is not in Jersey legislation (a contract, say): the Law does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"

§ `Article 7: amending subordinate legislation already amended`

-- Art 7(1) (src:83) [G-01]: a Law amended an Order; further amendment by other subordinate legislation is not limited.
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `a Law` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 7(1) [G-02]: a Law amended Regulations.
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `Regulations` `a Law` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 7(2) (src:84) [G-03]: Regulations amended an Order, which is not made by the States: treated as a Law for Art 7(1).
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `Regulations` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 7(2) [G-03]: Regulations amended another instrument not made by the States.
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` `Regulations` EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 7(2) (src:84) [G-04]: Regulations amended other Regulations (made by the States): Article 7(2) does not reach it; the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `Regulations` `Regulations`
-- Art 7(2) [G-04]: Regulations amended an Act of the States (made by the States).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` `Regulations`
-- Art 7(1) [G-05]: an Order amended an Order: not a Law, not Regulations; the Law says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `an Order`

§ `Article 8: consequential amendment of a Law`

-- Art 8(2) (src:89) [H-01]: A lodged 1 Mar and made 1 Jun 2022, B lodged 15 May and made 15 Jul 2022: the periods overlap.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 5 15) (YMD 2022 7 15) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-02]: A is made on the day B is lodged (1 Jun 2022): both end days are inside the periods.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 7 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-03]: B lodged the day after A was made: no overlap, Article 8 gives no power.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 6 2) (YMD 2022 7 1) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
-- Art 8(2) [H-04]: B made on the day A was lodged (1 Mar 2022): overlap.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-05]: B made the day before A was lodged: no overlap.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2022 2 28) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
-- Art 8(1) (src:86) [H-06]: B's period inside A's.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 4 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(1) [H-07]: A's period inside B's.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 4 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(1) [H-08]: identical periods.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-09]: both lodged and made on 1 Mar 2022.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-10]: single-day periods on 1 Mar and 2 Mar 2022.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 2) (YMD 2022 3 2) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
-- Art 8(2) [H-11]: A made 28 Feb 2024, B lodged 29 Feb 2024 (leap day).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 3 31) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
-- Art 8(2) [H-12]: A made 28 Feb 2024, B lodged 28 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 28) (YMD 2024 3 31) EQUALS TRUE
-- Art 8(2) [H-13]: A made 31 Dec 2022, B lodged 1 Jan 2023.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 10 1) (YMD 2022 12 31) (YMD 2023 1 1) (YMD 2023 3 1) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
-- Art 8(1) [H-14]: the test is symmetric: swap the Laws of H-02.
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 7 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) EQUALS TRUE

§ `UNSURE: the author could not decide between two readings; each assertion states the reading the author would take`

-- UNSURE [B-04] Art 2(1), 2(4) (src:32-35, 42): adopted and registered but never sanctioned. 2(1) says "and" (not made); 2(4) alone says made once registered. Taken: not made.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) (`ind: law steps` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 4 12)) FALSE) EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
-- UNSURE [C-38] Art 3(6), 3(2), 26 (src:54, 48, 223): legislation that commenced on 28 Sep 2021, the day Part 2 commenced. Reading A: Art 3(2) puts Part 2's start at the beginning of that day, so Article 3 governs. Reading B: the Law gives no instant for its own commencement, so "before" is not decided. Taken: B.
-- Moved after the first run (NOTES.md section 10.3): the exported question uses fork L3's default (reading A), so reading B, which the author took, is asserted on the rule module with L3's refusing reading.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28)) `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
-- UNSURE [E-12] Art 5(1), 5(5) (src:66, 79): legislation that expires with nothing repealing it. 5(1) is triggered by "Jersey legislation repeals", 5(5) says repeal includes expiry, and the heading says "repeal and expiry". Taken: Article 5 applies, so accrued rights survive.
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it expired` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
